From bcc18b85e412d7d9888bf82227750bf921b0e76b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 14:27:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 21/25] misc hardening: smb.conf snprintf, temp-file race,
 nvparse, urlfilter, SystemCmd (M6/M9/M19/L1/L5)

- M6 (libdisk/write_smb_conf.c): three snprintf(br0_ll/br0_unicast/
  br0_unicast_prefix, "%s", ...) calls were missing the size argument
  entirely (the "%s" was being passed as the size) -> unbounded write into
  [64] buffers. Add sizeof(dest).
- M9 (rc/common.c): remove_ip_rules() wrote `ip rule show > /tmp/iprule_tmp`
  as root to a fixed, predictable path (symlink race). Create the file with
  mkstemp() (O_EXCL, unique name) and read it back via the same fd.
- M19 (shared/nvparse.c): get_filter_url() used strncpy(value,
  nvram_get(name), sizeof(value)) -- NULL-deref risk and no NUL-term. Use
  strlcpy(nvram_safe_get()).
- L1 (rc/firewall_sdn.c): a URL-filter keyword was emitted verbatim into
  iptables --url/--string "%s" rules and an ip6tables doSystem(); add
  _urlf_keyword_safe() and skip keywords containing " \ ` $ or control/CR/LF
  so a crafted keyword can't break the quoting, run a shell, or inject a
  rule line.
- L5 (httpd/web.c): the four strncpy(SystemCmd, system_cmd, sizeof) calls
  left SystemCmd unterminated on a 128-byte input; use strlcpy.

Compile-verified (real userspace toolchain): common.o, firewall_sdn.o,
nvparse.o clean at the edit sites. write_smb_conf.c (libdisk) and web.c
edits syntax-checked (libdisk has no single-.o target; web.c full build is
blocked by the openssl generated-header cascade -- both environmental).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
